LOGIN(1)

NAME
    login - authenticate and start a SmallOS shell session

SYNOPSIS
    login [--] [user]

DESCRIPTION
    login is the native SmallOS console login program. Normal boot launches
    /bin/login after the filesystem, splash, input, and welcome summary are
    ready.

    With no user argument, login prompts:

        SmallOS login:

    The default image stages root through /etc/passwd and /etc/shadow:

        /etc/passwd: root:x:0:0:root:/:/bin/shell
        /etc/shadow: root::0:0:99999:7:::

    An empty shadow password logs in without a password prompt. A non-empty
    SmallOS shadow hash prompts for "Password:" with terminal echo disabled.
    Locked entries starting with ! or * and unsupported hash formats are
    rejected with "Login incorrect".

    On success, login applies the account uid, gid, HOME, USER, LOGNAME, and
    SHELL values, changes to the account home directory, and execs the account
    shell. When that shell exits, the boot sequence starts login again.

EXAMPLES
    login root
    login -- root

FILES
    /bin/login
    /etc/passwd
    /etc/shadow
    /etc/group
    /bin/shell

SEE ALSO
    passwd(1), shell(1), sh(1), busybox(1)
